From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dri: with a throttle depth, a short wait for the swap before
 (NUUBOS_THROTTLE_SOFT_MS)

With NUUBOS_THROTTLE_DEPTH 2 or 3 a swap waits only for the fence 2 or 3
swaps back, so a frame can reach the compositor while the GPU still has
the frame before it queued: on Dead or Alive 2 (Flycast, Mali-G31) such
frames missed their vblank, the compositor sent the next frame callback
two vblanks later and frames went out in pairs (31-38 % of frame
intervals over 20 ms at a depth of 2, 4 % at a depth of 1, same frame
rate). NUUBOS_THROTTLE_SOFT_MS=N (0-16) makes the swap first wait up to N
ms for the swap before, then for the deeper one as before: a GPU that
keeps up gives the pacing of a depth of 1, a GPU that is the limit still
gets the deeper queue. Without the variable nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_drawable.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_drawable.c
@@ -542,6 +542,16 @@
       unsigned depth = ctx->screen->throttle_depth;
       struct pipe_fence_handle **oldest = depth >= 2 ?
          &drawable->throttle_fence_old[depth - 2] : &drawable->throttle_fence;
+      /* nuubOS, NUUBOS_THROTTLE_SOFT_MS: with a depth of 2 or 3 the swap
+       * first waits that long for the swap before as well. A frame whose
+       * GPU work queued behind the one before was still being drawn when
+       * the compositor wanted it, missed its vblank and the frames went
+       * out in pairs (Dead or Alive 2: 31-38 % of frames over 20 ms at a
+       * depth of 2, 4 % at 1). When the GPU itself is the limit the wait
+       * runs out and the deeper queue keeps the frame rate. */
+      if (depth >= 2 && ctx->screen->throttle_soft_ns && drawable->throttle_fence)
+         screen->fence_finish(screen, NULL, drawable->throttle_fence,
+                              ctx->screen->throttle_soft_ns);
       if (*oldest) {
          screen->fence_finish(screen, NULL, *oldest, OS_TIMEOUT_INFINITE);
          screen->fence_reference(screen, oldest, NULL);
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
@@ -644,6 +644,7 @@
 
    screen->throttle = pscreen->caps.throttle;
    screen->throttle_depth = CLAMP(debug_get_num_option("NUUBOS_THROTTLE_DEPTH", 1), 1, 3);
+   screen->throttle_soft_ns = (uint64_t)CLAMP(debug_get_num_option("NUUBOS_THROTTLE_SOFT_MS", 0), 0, 16) * 1000000;
    if (pscreen->caps.device_protected_context)
       screen->has_protected_context = true;
    screen->has_reset_status_query = pscreen->caps.device_reset_status_query;
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.h
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.h
@@ -94,6 +94,9 @@
    /* Swaps that may be in flight before a swap waits for the GPU: 1, or up
     * to 3 with NUUBOS_THROTTLE_DEPTH (nuubOS). */
    unsigned throttle_depth;
+   /* With a depth of 2 or 3, how long a swap first waits for the swap
+    * before (NUUBOS_THROTTLE_SOFT_MS, nuubOS); 0 = not at all. */
+   uint64_t throttle_soft_ns;
    bool dmabuf_import;
 
    struct st_config_options options;
